hi welcome to part 5 of game theory in  breaking bad  the background of the scene is that  jesse  has tried to confront the people  that ripped off one of his dealers  in a series of events jesse bungles the  operation and he's almo he's held at  gunpoint  but he luckily escapes when one of the  drug addicts takes out the other in a  fit of rage  jesse is an absolute wreck after this  he's witnessed the murder of someone he  feels that life isn't valuable and he's  trying to consult he consoles himself by  taking drugs  he thinks the entire thing is over and  he doesn't want to do anything more  walt comes in  and he explains why the situation  actually worked out to their advantage  here's the clip  the point of the scene  is to demonstrate the power of  reputation  and that the concepts of breakage and  blowfish  are complementary  when jesse was being stolen from when he  had breakage  the problem is that one robbery can  inspire others  and the rep the lesson there is that if  others think you are weak then that  itself is a weakness they will try and  test you  you have to put more effort to defending  yourself  on the flip side  is the advantage of being a blowfish  you appear to be tougher than you are  and no one can really tell that  so  the lesson here  is that if others think you are strong  then that itself is a strength  so jesse  should not feel uh  he should actually feel very happy  about what happened and walt explains  that he's a blowfish  he doesn't have to actually create this  reputation  someone has done that for him  i want to thank you for watching this  five part series on game theory and  breaking bad  there are many many more examples of  game theory in the show i just wanted to  highlight five of the examples to get  you started  and i also want to make an interesting  connection  in the show walt is a chemistry teacher  and his job is to be familiar with the  actions and reactions between chemicals  but there is a corresponding point which  is that wall is also a game theorist and  shows that he can calculate the actions  reactions and counter reactions between  people  thanks for watching this series please  subscribe to my channel and you can  catch me on my blog mindyourdecisions or  on twitter at preshtalwalker
 

